{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>For</b> — \"Restore us speedily\"; rather, \"if You have utterly rejected us, [then] You have already raged against us with great rage.\" And it seems right to me that it reads: \"For if You have utterly rejected us, [then] You have already raged against us more than enough.\" And may He in His mercy have mercy upon us and upon the wretched, and may He establish the Prince Michael to plead good on behalf of Israel, and may the Redeemer come to Zion:"], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Resolved להיותו as 'that it reads,' referring to the verse's wording; the final clauses are prayers appended to the interpretation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:16.938633727Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}